addressbook><name>IKEDA, NOBUKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAGATSUME, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOIZUMI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MINAMI, YUKIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORIMOTO, AKIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAOKA, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHINO, KOUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHMI, TADAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIYAMA, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UENOYAMA, TOYOMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UNO, TOMIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAJI, MICHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YONEHANA, KATSUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A fluid feeding device having a plurality of flow paths disposed in parallel with each other starting at a regulator for pressure regulation, wherein a mass flow controller for flow control or a pressure system flow control device is disposed in each flow path so that the opening and closing operations for fluid supply in each flow path do not provide a transient variation in a stable supply to the other flow paths and, when the fluid supply in a flow path is changed from close to open, a set flow rate is reached a specified delay time after the start of the operation of the mass flow controller in that flow path.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif d'alimentation en fluide comportant une pluralité de voies d'écoulement disposées parallèlement les unes aux autres, et partant d'un régulateur de manière à réguler la pression. Le dispositif est caractérisé en ce qu'un contrôleur de débit massique permettant de réguler l'écoulement ou de commander le dispositif de régulation d'écoulement du système de pression est disposé dans chaque voie d'écoulement, de manière que les opérations d'ouverture et de fermeture de l'alimentation en fluide de chacune des voies ne produisent pas de variation transitoire de l'alimentation stable des autres voies d'écoulement, et que lorsque l'alimentation en fluide d'une voie d'écoulement est ouverte après fermeture, on atteigne un débit déterminé après un laps de temps défini à la suite de l'entrée en fonction du contrôleur de débit massique dans ladite voie d'écoulement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>